*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* XAOPS  -  ESA/390 INSTRUCTIONS FOR AN ASSEMBLER THAT PREDATES THEM  *
*                                                                     *
* VM/370 CE'S ASSEMBLER IS FROM THE 1970S.  THE CHANNEL SUBSYSTEM     *
* ARRIVED WITH 370-XA IN 1983 AND BSM WITH THE 31-BIT ADDRESSING      *
* FACILITY THE SAME YEAR, SO NONE OF THESE MNEMONICS ARE KNOWN TO IT. *
* RATHER THAN CHANGE THE TOOLCHAIN, EACH ONE IS A MACRO EMITTING ITS  *
* OWN ENCODING.                                                       *
*                                                                     *
* THE S-TYPE ADDRESS CONSTANT  S(EXPR)  PRODUCES THE 4-BIT BASE AND   *
* 12-BIT DISPLACEMENT THAT AN S-FORMAT INSTRUCTION WANTS, RESOLVED    *
* THROUGH THE ACTIVE USING.  SO THESE BEHAVE EXACTLY LIKE THE REAL    *
* INSTRUCTIONS, INCLUDING BASE REGISTER SELECTION.                    *
*                                                                     *
* DS 0H FIRST IN EVERY MACRO: THE S-TYPE CONSTANT FORCES HALFWORD     *
* ALIGNMENT, SO WITHOUT IT A MISALIGNED DC WOULD HAVE A PAD BYTE      *
* INSERTED BETWEEN THE OPCODE AND THE OPERAND.  IN AN INSTRUCTION     *
* STREAM THAT CANNOT NORMALLY HAPPEN, BUT IT COSTS NOTHING TO BE SURE.*
*                                                                     *
* BUILD:   MACLIB GEN XALIB XAOPS                                     *
* USE:     GLOBAL MACLIB XALIB DMSSP CMSLIB                           *
*                                                                     *
* ALL FOUR INSTRUCTIONS NEEDED TO DRIVE A DEVICE -- MSCH, SSCH, TSCH  *
* AND STSCH -- PLUS BSM HAVE BEEN EXECUTED SUCCESSFULLY UNDER HERCULES*
* 3.07 IN ESA/390 MODE FROM HAND-ASSEMBLED BYTES, SO THEIR ENCODINGS  *
* ARE PROVEN BY RUNNING, NOT ONLY BY READING.  SEE THE VERIFICATION   *
* NOTES AT THE END FOR WHICH ARE WHICH.                               *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
         MACRO
&LAB     SSCH  &ORB
.*  START SUBCHANNEL.  R1 MUST HOLD X'0001' IN THE HIGH HALFWORD AND
.*  THE SUBCHANNEL NUMBER IN THE LOW.  THE ORB MUST BE WORD ALIGNED
.*  AND -- THIS IS A HERCULES QUIRK, NOT ARCHITECTURE -- 32 BYTES OF
.*  ADDRESSABLE STORAGE MUST EXIST THERE EVEN WHEN THE EXTENSION BIT
.*  IS ZERO AND THE ARCHITECTED BLOCK IS ONLY 12 BYTES LONG.
.*  CC 0 ACCEPTED, 1 STATUS PENDING, 2 BUSY,
.*  CC 3 SUBCHANNEL NOT ENABLED OR LPM AND PAM DISJOINT.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B233',S(&ORB)
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     MSCH  &SCHIB
.*  MODIFY SUBCHANNEL.  READS 28 BYTES -- THE PMCW ONLY.  MANDATORY
.*  BEFORE THE FIRST SSCH ON ANY SUBCHANNEL, BECAUSE A SUBCHANNEL IS
.*  CREATED VALID BUT NOT ENABLED, AND SSCH ON A DISABLED SUBCHANNEL
.*  RETURNS CC 3 WITH NO EXCEPTION AND NO MESSAGE OF ANY KIND.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B232',S(&SCHIB)
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     STSCH &SCHIB
.*  STORE SUBCHANNEL.  THE SAFE WAY TO REACH MSCH IS STSCH, THEN SET
.*  THE ENABLE BIT IN THE STORED PMCW, THEN MSCH -- THAT CANNOT GET
.*  THE RESERVED BITS OF FLAG4, FLAG26 OR FLAG27 WRONG, EACH OF WHICH
.*  IS AN OPERAND EXCEPTION.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B234',S(&SCHIB)
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     TSCH  &IRB
.*  TEST SUBCHANNEL.  STORES 64 BYTES: SCSW, ESW, ECW.  SSCH IS
.*  ASYNCHRONOUS, SO THE FIRST TSCH AFTER IT NORMALLY GIVES CC 1 --
.*  LOOP, AND BOUND THE LOOP SO A STALL IS DIAGNOSABLE.
.*  CC 0 STATUS WAS PENDING AND HAS BEEN CLEARED, 1 NONE PENDING,
.*  CC 3 NOT OPERATIONAL.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B235',S(&IRB)
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     CSCH
.*  CLEAR SUBCHANNEL.  NO STORAGE OPERAND, BUT THE ENCODING STILL
.*  CARRIES A BASE-DISPLACEMENT FIELD, WHICH IS IGNORED.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B230',X'0000'
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     HSCH
.*  HALT SUBCHANNEL.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B231',X'0000'
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     RSCH
.*  RESUME SUBCHANNEL.  THE COUNTERPART OF S/370 RESUME I/O.
.*  OPCODE CONFIRMED BY TWO INDEPENDENT SOURCES -- SEE END OF FILE.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B238',X'0000'
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     TPI   &ADDR
.*  TEST PENDING INTERRUPTION.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B236',S(&ADDR)
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     SAL
.*  SET ADDRESS LIMIT.  IBM ADDED PER-SUBCHANNEL ADDRESS-LIMIT
.*  CHECKING SPECIFICALLY FOR VIRTUAL MACHINES, TO STOP A GUEST'S
.*  CHANNEL PROGRAM REACHING BEYOND ITS ASSIGNED STORAGE.  LIKELY TO
.*  MATTER FOR CP EVENTUALLY.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B237',X'0000'
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     STCRW &ADDR
.*  STORE CHANNEL REPORT WORD.  PART OF THE MACHINERY THAT REPLACES
.*  S/370 CHANNEL LOGOUT, SO IT BELONGS TO THE ERROR-RECOVERY REWRITE
.*  RATHER THAN TO NORMAL I/O.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B239',S(&ADDR)
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     BSM   &R1,&R2
.*  BRANCH AND SET MODE.  RR FORMAT.
.*
.*  TWO DISTINCT USES, AND THE SECOND IS NOT OBVIOUS:
.*
.*  BSM  0,RX   -- BRANCH TO RX, TAKING THE ADDRESSING MODE FROM ITS
.*                 BIT 0.  ONE MEANS 31-BIT, ZERO MEANS 24-BIT.
.*
.*  BSM  RY,0   -- WITH R2 ZERO NO BRANCH IS TAKEN AT ALL, AND THE
.*                 INSTRUCTION ONLY REPORTS THE CURRENT MODE IN BIT 0
.*                 OF RY, WHICH IS THE SIGN BIT.  SO  SR RY,RY  THEN
.*                 BSM RY,0  THEN  LTR RY,RY  TESTS THE MODE WITHOUT
.*                 NEEDING ANY ADDRESS ABOVE THE 16 MB LINE.  THAT
.*                 MATTERS, BECAUSE EVERY TEST THAT DISTINGUISHES THE
.*                 MODES BY TRUNCATION NECESSARILY USES ONE.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'0B',AL1((&R1)*16+(&R2))
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     BASSM &R1,&R2
.*  BRANCH AND SAVE AND SET MODE.  RR FORMAT.  SAVES THE RETURN
.*  ADDRESS IN R1 WITH ITS BIT 0 SET TO THE CALLER'S MODE, SO THE
.*  CALLEE CAN RETURN WITH  BSM 0,R1  AND RESTORE IT.  THIS IS THE
.*  INSTRUCTION A MIXED-MODE CALLING CONVENTION IS BUILT ON.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'0C',AL1((&R1)*16+(&R2))
         MEND
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* ESA/390 DAT INSTRUCTIONS -- ADDED 27 SEPTEMBER 2026                 *
*                                                                     *
* XAPROBE.ASSEMBLE MEASURED WHICH MNEMONICS ASSEMBLER XF ACTUALLY     *
* KNOWS RATHER THAN GUESSING.  THESE ARE THE ONES IT DOES NOT.        *
* PTLB IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT: IT IS S/370 (B20D) AND XF ALREADY      *
* KNOWS IT, WHICH THE PROBE CONFIRMED.                                *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
         MACRO
&LAB     IPTE  &R1,&R2
.*  INVALIDATE PAGE TABLE ENTRY.  R1 HOLDS THE PAGE TABLE ORIGIN,
.*  R2 THE VIRTUAL ADDRESS WHOSE ENTRY IS TO BE INVALIDATED.  THIS
.*  IS THE INSTRUCTION DMKPTR NEEDS WHEN IT STEALS A FRAME: UNDER
.*  S/370 CP SETS THE INVALID BIT AND PURGES THE WHOLE TLB, WHICH
.*  IPTE MAKES UNNECESSARY.
.*  HERCULES MARKS THIS RRR, NOT RRE, BECAUSE Z/ARCHITECTURE ADDED
.*  AN R3 FIELD IN THE HIGH NIBBLE OF BYTE 2.  ESA/390 HAS NO R3,
.*  SO THAT BYTE IS ZERO -- WHICH IS ALSO HOW Z/ARCHITECTURE READS
.*  "NO R3 SPECIFIED", SO THE ENCODING IS FORWARD-COMPATIBLE.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B221',X'00',AL1((&R1)*16+(&R2))
         MEND
         MACRO
&NAME    GADR31 &R
.*  A GUEST ADDRESS IN &R, BY THE GUEST'S MODE: BITS 8-31 FOR A 24-BIT
.*  GUEST, BITS 1-31 FOR ONE WITH PSW BIT 32 ON.  R11 IS THE VMBLOK.
.*  REPLACES LA &R,0(,&R), WHICH DID THE FIRST IN AMODE 24 AND NEITHER
.*  IN AMODE 31.  SETS THE CONDITION CODE (TM, N).  M2 STEP 3.
&NAME    TM    VMPSW+4-VMBLOK(R11),X'80'  31-BIT GUEST ?
         BO    *+8            YES: ONLY BIT 0 GOES
         N     &R,XRIGHT24    24-BIT GUEST: BYTE 0 GOES
         SLL   &R,1           BIT 0 OFF
         SRL   &R,1           ...
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     IPM   &R1
.*  INSERT PROGRAM MASK.  RRE.  PUTS THE CONDITION CODE IN BITS 2-3 OF
.*  R1 AND THE PROGRAM MASK IN BITS 4-7, BITS 0-1 ZERO, 8-31 UNCHANGED.
.*  CP SAVED THE CC WITH  BALR Rx,0  -- WHICH IN AMODE 24 LEAVES THE
.*  ILC, CC AND PM IN BYTE 0 OF Rx -- AND RESTORED IT WITH  SPM Rx.
.*  IN AMODE 31 BALR STORES BIT 0 AND A 31-BIT ADDRESS, NO CC AT ALL,
.*  SO SPM RESTORED CC 0 EVERY TIME (I-228: DMKLNK TOOK EVERY
.*  DIRECTORY LINK FOR 'ALREADY DEFINED').  IPM IS THE MODE-FREE FORM
.*  AND LEAVES THE SAME BITS WHERE SPM, STCM AND NI X'30' READ THEM.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B222',X'00',AL1((&R1)*16)
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     IVSK  &R1,&R2
.*  INSERT VIRTUAL STORAGE KEY.  RRE.  RETURNS THE KEY OF THE PAGE
.*  A VIRTUAL ADDRESS MAPS TO, WITHOUT CP HAVING TO TRANSLATE THE
.*  ADDRESS FIRST AND THEN ISSUE ISKE.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B223',X'00',AL1((&R1)*16+(&R2))
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     TPROT &OP1,&OP2
.*  TEST PROTECTION.  SSE FORMAT -- TWO STORAGE OPERANDS, SIX BYTES
.*  IN ALL.  OP1 IS THE ADDRESS TESTED, OP2 CARRIES THE ACCESS KEY
.*  IN BITS 24-27.  THE CONDITION CODE DISTINGUISHES FETCH-ONLY FROM
.*  STORE-PERMITTED FROM TRANSLATION-UNAVAILABLE, SO IT ANSWERS IN
.*  ONE INSTRUCTION WHAT CP CURRENTLY DISCOVERS BY TAKING A
.*  PROTECTION EXCEPTION.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'E501',S(&OP1),S(&OP2)
         MEND
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* ESA/390 STORAGE KEYS AT 4 KB                                        *
*                                                                     *
* CP USES ISK, SSK AND RRB, WHICH ADDRESS A 2 KB BLOCK.  UNDER        *
* ESA/390 A KEY COVERS A WHOLE 4 KB PAGE AND THESE ARE THE            *
* INSTRUCTIONS THAT REACH IT.  RISK R-12 IS THAT A GUEST READING      *
* ITS OWN KEYS THROUGH ISK STILL EXPECTS 2 KB SEMANTICS, SO DMKPRV    *
* WILL HAVE TO SIMULATE THE OLD VIEW ON TOP OF THE NEW ONE.           *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
         MACRO
&LAB     ISKE  &R1,&R2
.*  INSERT STORAGE KEY EXTENDED.  RRE.  THE 4 KB COUNTERPART OF ISK.
.*  PROVEN BY EXECUTION IN 11-storage-keys.rc.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B229',X'00',AL1((&R1)*16+(&R2))
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     SSKE  &R1,&R2
.*  SET STORAGE KEY EXTENDED.  THE 4 KB COUNTERPART OF SSK, AND THE
.*  INSTRUCTION THAT MAKES CP-67 STYLE READ-ONLY FRAME SHARING WORK:
.*  SHARED FRAMES GET KEY 0, THE SHARING MACHINES RUN AT PSW KEY F.
.*  HERCULES MARKS THIS RRF_M -- Z/ARCHITECTURE PUT A CONDITIONAL-SSKE
.*  MASK IN THE HIGH NIBBLE OF BYTE 2.  ESA/390 LEAVES IT ZERO.
.*  PROVEN BY EXECUTION IN 11-storage-keys.rc.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B22B',X'00',AL1((&R1)*16+(&R2))
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     RRBE  &R1,&R2
.*  RESET REFERENCE BIT EXTENDED.  THE 4 KB COUNTERPART OF RRB, AND
.*  DMKPTR'S PAGE-REPLACEMENT SCAN RUNS ON IT.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B22A',X'00',AL1((&R1)*16+(&R2))
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     TB    &R1,&R2
.*  TEST BLOCK.  TESTS A 4 KB FRAME FOR USABILITY AND CLEARS IT.
.*  NOT NEEDED BY ANY MILESTONE; INCLUDED BECAUSE IT SITS IN THE SAME
.*  OPCODE BLOCK AND THE PROBE SHOWED XF DOES NOT KNOW IT EITHER.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B22C',X'00',AL1((&R1)*16+(&R2))
         MEND
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* THE REST OF THE CHANNEL-SUBSYSTEM BLOCK                             *
*                                                                     *
* THE MACROS ABOVE STOP AT B239.  B23A THROUGH B23C ARE CHANNEL-PATH  *
* AND MONITOR CONTROL.  RISK R-03 -- CHANNEL LOGOUT HAS NO ESA/390    *
* EQUIVALENT -- IS WHY THEY ARE HERE: STCRW PLUS THESE ARE WHAT       *
* REPLACES TM CSW,X'04' AND THE LIMITED CHANNEL LOGOUT.               *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
         MACRO
&LAB     STCPS &ADDR
.*  STORE CHANNEL PATH STATUS.  STORES 32 BYTES.  THE ONE OF THE
.*  THREE WITH A REAL STORAGE OPERAND.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B23A',S(&ADDR)
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     RCHP
.*  RESET CHANNEL PATH.  USES GR1; NO STORAGE OPERAND -- HERCULES
.*  MARKS IT "none".  THIS IS THE INSTRUCTION THE B23B MISREADING IN
.*  I-21 ACTUALLY NAMED.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B23B',X'0000'
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     SCHM
.*  SET CHANNEL MONITOR.  USES GR1 AND GR2; NO STORAGE OPERAND.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B23C',X'0000'
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     XSCH
.*  CANCEL SUBCHANNEL.  USES GR1; NO STORAGE OPERAND.  CANCELS A START
.*  FUNCTION THAT HAS NOT YET BEEN PASSED TO THE DEVICE -- SOMETHING
.*  S/370 HAD NO EQUIVALENT OF, SINCE SIO EITHER STARTED OR DID NOT.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B276',X'0000'
         MEND
         MACRO
&LAB     CHSC
.*  CHANNEL SUBSYSTEM CALL.  THE REQUEST BLOCK ADDRESS IS IN GR1, SO
.*  THERE IS NO STORAGE OPERAND.  HERCULES MARKS THIS RRE AND IGNORES
.*  THE REGISTER FIELDS, SO A ZERO LOW HALFWORD IS BOTH FORMS AT ONCE.
&LAB     DS    0H
         DC    X'B25F',X'0000'
         MEND
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* WITH XSCH AND CHSC THE CHANNEL SUBSYSTEM SET IS COMPLETE.           *
*                                                                     *
* XAFULL.ASSEMBLE PROBED ALL 351 MNEMONICS HERCULES MARKS AVAILABLE   *
* IN ESA/390 MODE.  186 ARE UNKNOWN TO ASSEMBLER XF.  THE 24 MACROS   *
* IN THIS FILE COVER EVERY ONE OF THOSE 186 THAT BELONGS TO THE       *
* CHANNEL SUBSYSTEM, TO DAT, OR TO THE 4 KB STORAGE KEYS.  THE OTHER  *
* 162 BELONG TO FACILITIES CP DOES NOT USE -- THE VECTOR FACILITY     *
* (26), DECIMAL AND BINARY FLOATING POINT (64), ACCESS REGISTERS AND  *
* DUAL ADDRESS SPACE (32), Z/ARCHITECTURE ADDITIONS (32), EXPANDED    *
* STORAGE (4), BAS/BASR (2) AND TWO UNCLASSIFIED.                     *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* VERIFICATION STATUS                                                 *
*                                                                     *
* ACCEPTED BY CE ITSELF, 27 SEPTEMBER 2026.  THESE MACROS WERE READ   *
* ONTO MAINT 191 THROUGH THE CARD READER, BUILT WITH                  *
* MACLIB GEN XALIB XAOPS -- WHICH PRODUCED ALL TWELVE MEMBERS -- AND  *
* XATEST ASSEMBLED AGAINST THEM BY VM/370 CE'S OWN ASSEMBLER XF:      *
*                                                                     *
*     ASSEMBLER (XF) DONE                                             *
*     NO STATEMENTS FLAGGED IN THIS ASSEMBLY                          *
*     HIGHEST SEVERITY WAS    0                                       *
*     TOTAL RECORDS READ FROM SYSTEM LIBRARY      139                 *
*                                                                     *
* THE LIBRARY COUNT MATTERS: IT PROVES THE DEFINITIONS WERE FETCHED   *
* FROM XALIB RATHER THAN THE CALLS BEING QUIETLY IGNORED.             *
*                                                                     *
* AND EVERY S-TYPE CONSTANT RESOLVED CORRECTLY THROUGH THE USING.     *
* WITH  USING *,R15  ESTABLISHED AT X'02', SCHIB AT X'B8' ASSEMBLED   *
* AS F0B6 -- BASE R15, DISPLACEMENT X'0B6' = B8 - 02.  ORB, IRB AND   *
* PARM ARE ALL LIKEWISE EXACT.  THAT WAS THE ONE THING Z390 COULD     *
* NOT SETTLE, BECAUSE Z390 IS NOT THIS ASSEMBLER.                     *
*                                                                     *
* THE DS 0H PAID OFF TOO: EVERY GENERATED INSTRUCTION LANDED ON A     *
* HALFWORD BOUNDARY WITH NO PAD BYTE ANYWHERE IN THE SEQUENCE.        *
*                                                                     *
* FULL LISTING: validate/XATEST-CE-XF.LISTING                         *
*                                                                     *
* OBJECT BYTES AS EMITTED BY ASSEMBLER XF:                            *
*                                                                     *
*     STSCH  B234F0B6      CSCH   B2300000      BSM R1,0    0B10      *
*     MSCH   B232F0B6      HSCH   B2310000      BSM 0,R4    0B04      *
*     SSCH   B233F096      RSCH   B2380000      BASSM       0CEF      *
*     TSCH   B235F0EA      SAL    B2370000                            *
*     TPI    B236F04E      STCRW  B239F04E                            *
*                                                                     *
* THE FOUR THAT NEED NO MACRO ASSEMBLED NATIVELY IN THE SAME RUN,     *
* CONFIRMING THE NOTE AT THE END OF THIS FILE:                        *
*                                                                     *
*     STOSM  AD04F052      LCTL   B711F04A                            *
*     STNSM  ACFBF052      STCTL  B60FF056                            *
*                                                                     *
* HOW THEY WERE ORIGINALLY SOURCED, KEPT FOR PROVENANCE:              *
*                                                                     *
*                                                                     *
* PROVEN BY EXECUTION.  THESE FIVE RAN CORRECTLY UNDER HERCULES 3.07, *
* ARCHMODE ESA/390, FROM HAND-ASSEMBLED BYTES POKED INTO REAL STORAGE.*
* MSCH ENABLED A SUBCHANNEL, SSCH STARTED A FORMAT-1 CHANNEL PROGRAM, *
* TSCH RETURNED CLEAN STATUS AND THE DEVICE WROTE ITS LINE; BSM       *
* SWITCHED INTO 31-BIT MODE AND BACK, CONFIRMED BOTH BY THE PSW AND BY*
* BSM R1,0 REPORTING THE MODE.                                        *
*                                                                     *
*     MSCH   B232        STSCH  B234        BSM    0B                 *
*     SSCH   B233        TSCH   B235                                  *
*                                                                     *
* NOT YET EXECUTED, BUT CONFIRMED BY A SECOND INDEPENDENT SOURCE --   *
* THE Z390 ASSEMBLER'S OPCODE TABLE (TZ390.JAVA), WHICH IS NOT        *
* DERIVED FROM HERCULES:                                              *
*                                                                     *
*     CSCH   B230        TPI    B236        RSCH   B238               *
*     HSCH   B231        SAL    B237        STCRW  B239               *
*     BASSM  0C                                                       *
*                                                                     *
* THE RSCH DISCREPANCY IS RESOLVED.  AN EARLIER READING OF THE 370-XA *
* REFERENCE SUMMARY GX20-0157-2 GAVE B23B FOR RSCH.  THAT WAS A       *
* CONFUSION BETWEEN TWO SIMILARLY-NAMED CHANNEL INSTRUCTIONS.  Z390'S *
* TABLE LISTS THE WHOLE BLOCK CONTIGUOUSLY:                           *
*                                                                     *
*     B238 RSCH    B239 STCRW   B23A STCPS   B23B RCHP   B23C SCHM    *
*                                                                     *
* B23B IS RCHP -- RESET CHANNEL PATH -- A DIFFERENT INSTRUCTION WITH A*
* RELATED PURPOSE, WHICH IS WHY IT WAS MISREAD AS RSCH.  RSCH IS B238.*
*                                                                     *
* CSCH, HSCH, RSCH AND SAL TAKE NO STORAGE OPERAND -- HERCULES MARKS  *
* THEM ASMFMT_NONE -- SO THEIR LOW HALFWORD IS IGNORED AND IS EMITTED *
* AS X'0000' RATHER THAN THROUGH AN S-TYPE CONSTANT.                  *
*                                                                     *
* HOW TO CHECK ANY OF THEM.  ASSEMBLE A ONE-LINE TEST, THEN READ THE  *
* OBJECT BYTES FROM THE LISTING -- THE FIRST TWO SHOULD MATCH THE     *
* TABLE ABOVE.  OR LOAD THE MODULE UNDER HERCULES WITH  T+  AND LET IT*
* DISASSEMBLE, WHICH IS HOW THE FIVE ABOVE WERE CONFIRMED.            *
*                                                                     *
* NOT INCLUDED, AND WHY                                               *
*                                                                     *
* STOSM AND STNSM NEED NO MACRO.  THEY EXIST IN S/370 EC MODE AND CE'S*
* ASSEMBLER ALREADY KNOWS THEM -- CP ITSELF USES EACH FIVE TIMES.     *
*                                                                     *
* LCTL AND STCTL LIKEWISE: CP USES THEM 172 AND 28 TIMES.             *
*                                                                     *
* SAM24, SAM31 AND SAM64 ARE Z/ARCHITECTURE, NOT ESA/390.  IN ESA/390 *
* THE ADDRESSING MODE IS CHANGED WITH BSM OR BASSM.                   *
*                                                                     *
* IPTE, IVSK AND TPROT USED TO BE LISTED HERE AS "NOT NEEDED YET".    *
* THEY ARE NOW DEFINED ABOVE, ALONG WITH THE 4 KB KEY INSTRUCTIONS    *
* AND THE REST OF THE CHANNEL BLOCK.  XAPROBE.ASSEMBLE MEASURED THE   *
* GAP INSTEAD OF GUESSING AT IT, AND THE GUESS HAD BEEN WRONG IN      *
* BOTH DIRECTIONS: PTLB WAS ASSUMED MISSING AND IS NOT, WHILE TB,     *
* RCHP, STCPS AND SCHM WERE NOT ON THE LIST AT ALL.                   *
*                                                                     *
* STILL DELIBERATELY ABSENT, ALL MEASURED UNKNOWN TO XF AND NONE      *
* NEEDED BY ANY MILESTONE:                                            *
*                                                                     *
*     LHI  AHI  CHI  MHI        HALFWORD IMMEDIATE ARITHMETIC         *
*     BRAS BRC                  RELATIVE BRANCHING                    *
*     MVST CLST SRST CUSE       STRING INSTRUCTIONS                   *
*     LURA STURA                REAL-ADDRESS LOAD AND STORE           *
*     STCKE                     STORE CLOCK EXTENDED                  *
*     TRACE                     TRACE                                 *
*                                                                     *
* THAT LIST IS WORTH KNOWING FOR A PRACTICAL REASON.  WITHOUT         *
* RELATIVE BRANCHES OR HALFWORD IMMEDIATES, EVERY NEW SEQUENCE        *
* WRITTEN FOR THE CONVERSION NEEDS A BASE REGISTER AND A LITERAL      *
* POOL, EXACTLY AS THE REST OF CP DOES.  NEW CODE CANNOT BE WRITTEN   *
* IN A MORE MODERN STYLE THAN THE CODE AROUND IT.                     *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
